# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This checkout had core.autocrlf=true, so Git stored LF and handed out CRLF.
# Two things followed, both of which cost real time:
#
#   Every build rewrote public/sitemap.xml and docs/ROUTE-INVENTORY.md with LF,
#   Git saw a change against the CRLF copy, and `npm run deploy` refused to
#   publish because the tree was dirty. Nothing had actually changed.
#
#   check-root-entry asserts a pattern that spans a newline. It passed on the
#   machine whose checkout had LF and failed on the one that had CRLF, from the
#   same commit. A build whose result depends on which operating system cloned
#   the repository is not telling you about the code.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises on the way in and checks out LF regardless of
# core.autocrlf, so both stop happening for everyone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.zip binary
